            "text": "A flaw was found in libsoup. When constructing a masked WebSocket client frame for a very large outgoing payload, size values passed to GByteArray allocation APIs could be truncated while the masking routine still used the full length, causing a heap buffer overflow.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "libsoup: libsoup: Heap buffer overflow during WebSocket client-frame masking",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "This issue is rated Important. Triggering requires causing a libsoup WebSocket client (or client-role connection) to send an extremely large message. That may be reachable when application-level message size is attacker-influenced. Impact is heap corruption or denial of service in the sending process.",
            "title": "Statement"
          },
          {
            "category": "general",
            "text": "The CVSS score(s) listed for this vulnerability do not reflect the associated product's status, and are included for informational purposes to better understand the severity of this vulnerability.",
            "title": "CVSS score applicability"
          }
